  ('s-c-u-b-a-scooter-nb', 'S.C.U.B.A. Scooter', 'nightbane', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '3 knots', 50, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'UNDERWATER VEHICLES, printed 232. The book prints no price for any of the five. Capable of pulling one to three divers; the handles are designed to pull them with minimum stress on the arm muscles. Cylindrical, with a front mounted rotor. Length 3ft 1in (0.94m), width 1ft 5in, height 10 inches (0.25m); weight dry 57lbs (26kg), submerged 5oz (0.23kg). Maximum depth 300ft. Range 3 nautical miles. Works on the surface or submerged.', 'Nightbane RPG p.232'),
  ('s-c-u-b-a-scooter-platform-nb', 'S.C.U.B.A. Scooter Platform', 'nightbane', 'vehicle', NULL, 'One pilot, and can pull up to four more divers', NULL, NULL, '5 knots', 120, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'UNDERWATER VEHICLES, printed 232. The book prints no price for any of the five. A larger, more stable version of the little scooter that a diver can lie on top of to ride. Its basic purpose is to carry S.C.U.B.A. divers and their equipment into the sea and return them safely; it also serves as a precisely controlled stable platform for underwater photography. Length 9ft 3in (2.8m), 4ft (1.2m) fin tip to fin tip; weight 270lbs dry, 181lbs submerged. Maximum depth 1970ft (600m). Range 15 nautical miles. Cargo capacity 1000lbs (450kg).', 'Nightbane RPG p.232'),
  ('sea-sled-cav-nb', 'Sea Sled (CAV)', 'nightbane', 'vehicle', '2', NULL, NULL, NULL, '3 knots', 270, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'UNDERWATER VEHICLES, printed 232. The book prints no price for any of the five. CAV is Construction Assistance Vehicle. An underwater pickup truck capable of carrying up to 2000lbs (910kg) of wet weight cargo, with a two-seat cockpit and an open cargo bed in the rear (11 x 4.5 x 1.5ft). Length 27ft (8.23m). Maximum depth 150ft (45.7m). Range 15 miles (24km). Life support is 5 compressed air bottles, a 2 hour air supply. Can function on the surface or submerged.', 'Nightbane RPG p.232'),
  ('waterdinger-nb', 'Waterdinger', 'nightbane', 'vehicle', NULL, 'Two S.C.U.B.A. divers and equipment', NULL, NULL, '2 knots', 150, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'UNDERWATER VEHICLES, printed 232. The book prints no price for any of the five. A small diver assist vehicle. Length 7ft (2.1m). Maximum depth 300ft (91m). Range 4 nautical miles. Cargo capacity 750lbs dry (340kg).', 'Nightbane RPG p.232'),
  ('two-diver-submersible-transport-vehicle-nb', 'Two Diver Submersible Transport Vehicle', 'nightbane', 'vehicle', '2', NULL, NULL, NULL, '1.5 to 9 knots', 550, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'UNDERWATER VEHICLES, printed 232. The book prints no price for any of the five. A variety of two-man research submersibles with similar capabilities. Length 12 to 16ft (3.6m to 4.9m). Maximum depth 2000ft (610m). SPEED AND RANGE TRADE AGAINST EACH OTHER: at 1.5 knots the range is 100 miles (the book prints the metric figure as 160m), at 6 knots about 45 miles (72km), and at 9 knots 10 miles (16km). Life support endurance 18 hours plus 6 hours emergency.', 'Nightbane RPG p.232');
